config.prompt:
Analyze these SELinux AVC denials from a RHEL 10.2 system running httpd with content at /srv/webapp/ (non-standard). System was moved from disabled to permissive mode.

AVC Denials:
${trigger.payload.payload.payload.avc_denials}

audit2allow output:
${trigger.payload.payload.payload.audit2allow_output}

For each unique denial, determine the correct fix. Prefer relabeling (semanage fcontext + restorecon) over booleans or custom policy modules. audit2allow suggestions are often overly permissive.

Return JSON only:
{"summary":"...","findings":[{"denial":"what was denied","source_type":"e.g. httpd_t","target_type":"e.g. var_t","target_path":"/path","permission":"e.g. read","recommendation":"human-readable fix","remediation":{"type":"fcontext|boolean|port|module","selinux_type":"target type","path_spec":"regex for semanage","boolean_name":"","boolean_value":""}}],"audit2allow_assessment":"what it got right/wrong"}
